{
 "name": "Contraptions 18: Hilbert circuit (order 3, capacitor trap, small dots) (Momentum Bubbles 14)",
 "description": "A Hilbert-curve circuit (order 3, 63 gates, each aiming at the next) at 512\u00b2: 63 dots (radius 10 cells) start at rest in every 1th gate, which launch them along the curve into a trap on its last point (Momentum Bubbles 14), like a capacitor: a smooth round hill that brakes whatever comes in and draws it to its middle, senses how full it is, and once full (about 0.45 of it) lets go, sending what it collected straight east along the lowest row, round the frame into the first point, to go round again. Gates: brake, accel 0.002, aim_speed 0.025. Gates show as the aim channel, the trap as trap and full, in the custom palette. Found: the dots (about the smallest that hold together on the move; 8 cells breaks into specks) run the curve in step; the trap fires every ~20000-40000 steps, and what it releases is everything it gathered, merged into one big blob (~10 dots), which goes round collecting more: 63 dots become 18 bodies by 120000 steps, the small dots still small, the blobs bigger each time.",
 "rule": "builtin:53",
 "size": 512,
 "start": "initial",
 "stepsPerFrame": 40,
 "globals": {
  "aim_speed": 0.025,
  "brake": 0.002,
  "accel": 0.002,
  "full_at": 0.45
 },
